(loud sigh)

00:00:14.378 --> 00:00:15.870
- Okay. So I've been
investigating something

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:16.920
for a long time.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.300
Probably deeper than I've
gone on any other video

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.360
for a while at least.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.680
Something I never thought
I would be investigating,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.513
but I am.

00:00:23.513 --> 00:00:26.640
I'm investigating McDonald's
ice cream machines.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.840
Who wants to go get ice cream.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:28.673
- Me!

00:00:30.281 --> 00:00:31.114
- [McDonald Attendant]
Hello, can I take your order?

00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:32.617
- Can I get an ice cream cone?

00:00:32.617 --> 00:00:34.408
- [McDonald Attendant] We
don't have ice cream right now.

00:00:34.408 --> 00:00:35.507
- Not today.

00:00:35.507 --> 00:00:36.340
- [McDonald Attendant] Not today.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.173
- Maybe tomorrow or something?

00:00:37.173 --> 00:00:38.123
- [McDonald Attendant] Or
next week, I don't know.

00:00:38.123 --> 00:00:39.240
- Does that happen a lot?

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.357
Like that, the machine's down.

00:00:40.357 --> 00:00:41.885
- [McDonald Attendant]
Yeah. In this store yeah.

00:00:41.885 --> 00:00:42.718
- Okay.

00:00:42.718 --> 00:00:43.570
For a few years now

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:46.100
people have taken notice
that the ice cream machines

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.340
at McDonald's always seem to be down.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.010
- [Woman] The ice cream
machine part is not working.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.570
- The broken ice cream machines

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.440
at McDonald's have been the fodder

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.830
for a lot of weird internet culture.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.470
One guy even made an
interactive map that shows

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:03.730
every single McDonald's that
has a broken ice cream machine,

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:04.860
at this current moment.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.080
- So I reverse engineered the Android app.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.670
I think it was like, it was a meme

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:11.410
but nobody actually knew if
this meme was correct or not,

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.510
but they didn't know that was like an,

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:16.410
actual thing that all the
franchises are struggling with.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.550
- But a couple months ago, I got an email

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:22.460
from a guy who said that
he had a deeper story.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:24.100
He said that they're important questions

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.670
that no one is asking,

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:28.730
and he promised me answers
to those questions,

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.790
and data and evidence to back it up.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.730
He even said that there's potentially,

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.980
something nefarious going on here.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:35.813
- I was like,

00:01:35.813 --> 00:01:36.646
"Okay, cool.

00:01:36.646 --> 00:01:37.479
Another conspiracy theory

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:39.580
about these McDonald's ice cream makers."

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:42.340
So I asked my producer,
Jack, to get on the phone

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.480
with this guy and hear him out.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.158
A week later, Jack called me.

00:01:47.158 --> 00:01:49.270
- [Jack] And there's actually
something going on here.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:50.340
I've been going through everything

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.003
and you really need to see this.

00:01:52.003 --> 00:01:52.836
- Okay.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.183
I was still highly skeptical that

00:01:55.183 --> 00:01:58.880
this could be anything worth
a video or an investigation,

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.010
but I decided to dive in
anyway and see this evidence

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:02.843
for myself.

00:02:02.843 --> 00:02:06.610
I started looking at data at
internal McDonald's emails.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:10.300
At these mind numbing, 100
page instruction manuals

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.720
for ice cream makers.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.600
I started talking to
McDonald's franchise owners

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.640
and managers, and guess, it
turns out there is something

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.110
really weird going on here.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.840
Something that hasn't
been reported on before

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.100
and something that shows

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.630
that McDonald's broken ice cream machines

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:30.210
actually reveal a bigger story about

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.950
how big businesses protect one another.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.270
Even if that means
hurting their customers.

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.710
I never thought I'd be going
down a deep investigation

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:41.030
into ice cream makers, but I am.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:41.863
And I did.

00:02:41.863 --> 00:02:43.889
And I wanna share with you what I learned.

00:02:43.889 --> 00:02:45.220
(upbeat music)

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.460
- McDonald's is getting on (beep) nerves.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.000
- And that machine is always down.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.980
- The ice cream machine is broken.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.545
- And if you tried to pull
the lever, this what happens.

00:02:54.545 --> 00:02:55.573
(loud whirring)

00:02:55.573 --> 00:02:58.680
- Sorry, the ice cream machine is broken.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.650
The broken McDonald's ice
cream machine epidemic

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.650
has been so widespread for
so long that it's a meme.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:04.870
- [Man] You know what they're gonna say.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:08.687
You already know, "The ice
cream machine is broken."

00:03:08.687 --> 00:03:10.010
(hiphop music)

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.966
- Ice cream machine is broken.

00:03:11.966 --> 00:03:14.549
(hiphop music)

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.705
Kinda sounds like there's
a story behind that one,

00:03:18.705 --> 00:03:19.538
doesn't it?

00:03:19.538 --> 00:03:20.371
(crowd laughing)

00:03:20.371 --> 00:03:22.954
(gentle music)

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:26.110
- In this very moment,

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:29.140
if you look at McBroken, around 13%

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.840
of ice cream makers in the
United States are not working.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.580
That's any red dot on this map.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.980
What a brilliant little tool Rashiq made.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.530
I mean, this is just so good.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:41.590
So Jack, why are the ice
cream machines always broken?

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:43.640
- So once the internet
started to notice this,

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.620
the Wall Street Journal
and Business Insider

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.270
and a bunch of other outlets
started to report on it.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:49.800
And the conclusion that they came to

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.840
was that these machines
aren't actually broken,

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.730
they're just going through a really long

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.130
and really complicated cleaning cycle

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.937
that lasts four hours at a time.

00:03:58.937 --> 00:04:02.190
And when that happens, the
employees tell you it's broken

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.920
because it's just easier.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.990
But, don't take my word for it.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:06.840
- So when you go there

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.240
and they tell you it's broken,

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:09.860
there's a high chance it's not broken,

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:12.350
it's just shut up for maintenance.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:16.560
- Okay. So human error and
this long cleaning cycle,

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.080
that was the conclusion
that like everyone came to

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.970
and everyone seemed to
be satisfied with that.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.640
I mean, I would be satisfied with that.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:27.240
It's a pretty tight conclusion,
but hold on a second.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.214
Wait a minute.

00:04:28.214 --> 00:04:30.797
(upbeat music)

00:04:32.864 --> 00:04:33.697
- Do you guys have Frosties?

00:04:33.697 --> 00:04:34.530
- [Wendy's Attendant] Yeah.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:35.640
- I was just at McDonald's

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.490
and the ice cream machine was broken

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:39.510
and it seems like it always is.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.647
Is the ice cream machine
broken here very often?

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:42.650
- [Wendy's Attendant] No. Yeah.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.120
That's what McDonald's problem.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:45.820
We wash our machines every single--

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.000
- Oh, that's cool.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.354
Is it easy to do that or
is it pretty complicated?

00:04:49.354 --> 00:04:50.510
- [Wendy's Attendant] No,
it's actually really easy

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:51.343
to clean it.

00:04:51.343 --> 00:04:52.318
They're just lazy.

00:04:52.318 --> 00:04:53.970
(Johnny laughing)

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:54.803
It's the honest truth.

00:04:54.803 --> 00:04:55.860
That's the honest truth.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.960
- So, Wendy's doesn't have this problem.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.970
And what's crazy is that they
use the same brand of machine

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:05.140
as McDonald's does, and yet
they don't have a McBroken.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:08.370
It's not an internet
meme for them, nor is it

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.360
for other places that use the
same brand of ice cream maker,

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:15.470
like In-N-Out or Chick-fil-A
or a bunch of others.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:19.320
So, why is it only
McDonald's that has a problem

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:21.239
with the broken ice cream maker?

00:05:21.239 --> 00:05:22.253
- [Attendant] That's
only a McDonald's thing.

00:05:22.253 --> 00:05:23.306
We don't have that issue.

00:05:23.306 --> 00:05:24.414
- You don't have that issue here.

00:05:24.414 --> 00:05:25.247
- [Attendant] I promise.

00:05:25.247 --> 00:05:26.080
(Johnny laughing)

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:27.440
(gentle music)

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:29.880
- If you want a real answer on this,

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.470
you need to talk to the
people who suffer the most

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:35.130
when these machines' broken,

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:37.210
which actually isn't McDonald's corporate,

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:39.650
it's the people who own
these individual restaurants

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:40.930
or franchises.

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:43.160
These are the people who pay the price

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:46.170
in lost revenue, when
the machine is broken.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.120
So I talk to them.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:50.830
I talked to managers who actually
deal with broken machines

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:55.350
and I also went deep in this
111 page owner's manual,

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:57.810
which is not a read I recommend

00:05:57.810 --> 00:06:00.243
but I will summarize what it says.

00:06:00.243 --> 00:06:01.300
(gentle upbeat music)

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:05.690
What I've found is as mind
boggling as it is infuriating.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.710
To understand this, you have to understand

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:10.600
how these ice cream machines
work, and why they break.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.190
So I ask you to bear with me

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:14.170
as we learn how an ice cream machine

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.810
at McDonald's works, and
why they always break.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.150
Once you understand that

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:21.460
you will understand who is
getting rich every time one

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.180
of these things breaks,

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:26.109
and why they have an
incentive to keep them broken.

00:06:26.109 --> 00:06:28.660
(bright hiphop music)

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:29.493
- And I was like,

00:06:29.493 --> 00:06:32.437
"Okay. I'm gonna guess it's
gonna be around like 5%.

00:06:32.437 --> 00:06:36.510
And it came back to like
13%, which is insane.

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:38.977
- One question that needs to be asked is,

00:06:38.977 --> 00:06:41.270
"Should you be building
ice cream machines,

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:45.189
if after 17 years you still
can't get the software right?"

00:06:45.189 --> 00:06:47.360
(hiphop music)

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:50.430
- [Wendy's Attendant] No. Yeah,
that's a McDonald's problem.

